logs-dir

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Keep LocalBackend from creating a logs directory in a build without logtail: logpolicy.LogsDir, called only for the socket-statistics logger, makes ~/.local/share/tailscale for a non-root user even under ts_omit_logtail, where that logger is never made, so shephrd would write outside its instance directory.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream calls logpolicy.LogsDir only when the socket-statistics logger is compiled in, or stops LogsDir creating directories under ts_omit_logtail.
---
 ipn/ipnlocal/local.go |   10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ipn/ipnlocal/local.go b/ipn/ipnlocal/local.go
index d869979655142d6b2f85c397fff259ce031465f5..772e72cc7c3d348e11f5f4e79f53590e3579bcbe 100644
--- a/ipn/ipnlocal/local.go
+++ b/ipn/ipnlocal/local.go
@@ -653,9 +653,13 @@ func NewLocalBackend(logf logger.Logf, logID logid.PublicID, sys *tsd.System, lo
 	}()
 
 	netMon := sys.NetMon.Get()
-	b.sockstatLogger, err = sockstatlog.NewLogger(logpolicy.LogsDir(logf), logf, logID, netMon, sys.HealthTracker.Get(), sys.Bus.Get())
-	if err != nil {
-		logf("error setting up sockstat logger: %v", err)
+	// Without logtail there is no sockstat logger, and logpolicy.LogsDir would
+	// still create a directory on disk for it.
+	if buildfeatures.HasLogTail {
+		b.sockstatLogger, err = sockstatlog.NewLogger(logpolicy.LogsDir(logf), logf, logID, netMon, sys.HealthTracker.Get(), sys.Bus.Get())
+		if err != nil {
+			logf("error setting up sockstat logger: %v", err)
+		}
 	}
 	// Enable sockstats logs only on non-mobile unstable builds
 	if version.IsUnstableBuild() && !version.IsMobile() && b.sockstatLogger != nil {
